    "behavioral_notes": [
      {
        "element": "stock.picking.button_validate",
        "observation": "Confirms draft pickings, runs sanity checks and pre-action wizards, then calls _action_done. On partial fulfillment it splits demand and creates a backorder stock.picking (governed by picking_type_id.create_backorder = never/ask/always); the backorder wizard (stock.backorder.confirmation) is raised when _check_backorder finds unfulfilled demand. May also surface the reception report and trigger auto-print report actions. None of this is visible in metadata.",
        "source": "code-read"
      },
      {
        "element": "stock.quant._apply_inventory / _update_available_quantity",
        "observation": "Inventory adjustments do not edit a quantity in place: _apply_inventory generates compensating stock.move records between the location and the product's inventory-loss location, validates them via _action_done, then re-triggers reservation. _update_available_quantity is the single sudo entry point that increments/decrements quant quantity and reserved_quantity; all stock level changes funnel through quant writes. Stock is thus an append-only move ledger, not a mutable balance.",
        "source": "code-read"
      },
      {
        "element": "stock.rule._run_pull / _run_push",
        "observation": "stock.rule is the procurement engine: _run_pull turns a procurement (product, qty, dest location) into a sudo-created stock.move with the configured procure_method (make_to_stock vs make_to_order / mts_else_mto) and confirms it, which recursively launches upstream procurements; _run_push applies push rules after a move arrives. This is how stock.route chains multi-step flows (e.g. input->QC->stock, pick->pack->ship) and how an upstream sale/purchase demand pulls a delivery into being.",
        "source": "code-read"
      },
      {
        "element": "stock.move._action_assign (reservation)",
        "observation": "Reservation matches move demand against available stock.quant, creating/updating stock.move.line records and moving quantity into reserved_quantity; a move becomes 'assigned' or 'partially_available'. button_validate marks lines 'picked' and _action_done commits the physical move, updating both source and destination quants.",
        "source": "code-read"
      },
      {
        "element": "stock.warehouse / stock.warehouse.orderpoint automation",
        "observation": "Creating a warehouse auto-generates its location tree, picking types (in/out/int/pick/pack/qc/store/xdock) and reception/delivery routes per the multi-step reception_steps/delivery_steps settings (44 methods on stock.warehouse). Orderpoints (min/max reordering rules) run on a scheduler to compute qty_to_order and launch replenishment procurements through stock.rule.",
        "source": "code-read"
      },
      {
        "element": "frontend (OWL/JS)",
        "observation": "40 JS files, 20 OWL components, 29 registry registrations, 1 patches; asset bundles ['web.report_assets_common', 'web.assets_backend', 'web.assets_backend_lazy'].",
