  "classification": {
    "value_model": "chain",
    "activity_class": "primary",
    "apqc_category": "4.0 Deliver Physical Products",
    "rationale": "stock is the inbound and outbound logistics primary activity of the value chain (Porter): it physically receives, stores, moves and ships goods. The append-only stock.move ledger reconciled into stock.quant balances is classic value-chain transformation/flow. APQC 4.0 'Deliver Physical Products' covers it directly: 4.3.2.1 manage raw material inventory (stock.quant moves/valuation), 4.4.1.4 delivery service policy (stock.picking.type), and 4.4.x operate outbound transportation / ship (stock.picking.button_validate); replenishment touches 4.1.2.1 demand forecasts (stock.warehouse.orderpoint). It is primary, not support: goods physically flow through it to the customer."
  },
